From 897befb31545eee09f1c84dd65b823024ce87abd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 08:00:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] seo: enrich product structured data and fix duplicate meta
 descriptions
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Product JSON-LD now includes additionalProperty (from specs),
  itemCondition and availability (BackOrder, since nothing ships from
  local stock — see check-seo.js's forbidden-pattern guard).
- Fix a <title> duplication bug where seoTitle already carried the
  article and site name, but generateMetadata appended them again
  (titles were rendering 80-95 chars); now capped at ~70 chars for all
  578 products.
- Regenerate metaDescription for the 467 products that shared one of
  several generic per-category boilerplate strings (worst case: 254
  products with an identical description), building a unique summary
  from each product's title plus its top distinguishing specs
  (thread, tip/ball diameter and material, stem material, length,
  signal tech, protection class, etc). The 111 already-unique
  descriptions are untouched. All 578 products now have a distinct
  metaDescription.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KrwPjyGqrLYBmWMSvyn9JL
